# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Debugging and tracing for the latest version of Samplomatic"
msgstr "Debugging at tracing para sa pinakabagong bersyon ng Samplomatic"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Debugging and tracing"
msgstr "Debugging at tracing"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Debugging and tracing {#debugging-and-tracing}"
msgstr "Debugging at tracing {#debugging-and-tracing}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") function transforms an annotated circuit into a template circuit and samplex pair. In a complex circuit it can be hard to tell which box in the original circuit corresponds to which barriers in the template, or which nodes in the samplex DAG.\n"
msgstr "Ang function na [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") ay nagta-transform ng annotated na circuit tungo sa pares ng template circuit at samplex. Sa isang masalimuot na circuit, maaaring mahirap malaman kung aling box sa orihinal na circuit ang tumutugma sa aling mga barrier sa template, o aling mga node sa samplex DAG.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplomatic provides two complementary tracing tools:\n"
msgstr "Nagbibigay ang Samplomatic ng dalawang magkatuwang na tracing tool:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Barrier labels**: Every barrier in the template circuit carries a label that encodes its origin. These are always present regardless of whether `debug=True` is set.\n"
msgstr "**Mga barrier label**: Ang bawat barrier sa template circuit ay may label na nag-e-encode ng pinagmulan nito. Palagi itong naroroon, itinakda man o hindi ang `debug=True`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Trace info on samplex nodes**: When [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") is called with `debug=True`, every samplex node carries a `TraceInfo` object linking it back to the box or boxes that produced it.\n"
msgstr "**Trace info sa mga samplex node**: Kapag tinawag ang [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") na may `debug=True`, ang bawat samplex node ay may dalang `TraceInfo` object na nag-uugnay pabalik sa box o mga box na lumikha nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both tools are most useful when boxes carry a [`Tag`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tag#samplomatic.Tag \"samplomatic.Tag\") annotation, which attaches a `ref` string to the box. Alternatively, [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") references are also attached.\n"
msgstr "Pinakakapaki-pakinabang ang parehong tool kapag ang mga box ay may [`Tag`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tag#samplomatic.Tag \"samplomatic.Tag\") annotation, na nag-aattach ng `ref` string sa box. Bilang alternatibo, ina-attach din ang mga reference ng [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tag boxes {#tag-boxes}"
msgstr "Mga tag box {#tag-boxes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`Tag`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tag#samplomatic.Tag \"samplomatic.Tag\") annotation attaches a `ref` string to a box. The `ref` then appears in barrier labels and in trace information on samplex nodes.\n"
msgstr "Ang isang [`Tag`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tag#samplomatic.Tag \"samplomatic.Tag\") annotation ay nag-aattach ng `ref` string sa isang box. Lumalabas ang `ref` sa mga barrier label at sa trace information sa mga samplex node.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following example circuit has three boxes: two tagged CX boxes on disjoint qubit pairs, and an untagged right-dressed measurement box. The second CX box also carries an [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") annotation — both its `tag` ref and its noise `ref` will appear in the barrier labels. The two CX boxes cover different qubits, which enables the samplex optimizer to merge their propagation nodes into shared nodes. This is shown in the trace information section.\n"
msgstr "Ang sumusunod na halimbawang circuit ay may tatlong box: dalawang naka-tag na CX box sa magkahiwalay na qubit pair, at isang walang tag na right-dressed na measurement box. Ang ikalawang CX box ay may dala ring [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") annotation — parehong ang `tag` ref at ang noise `ref` nito ay lalabas sa mga barrier label. Ang dalawang CX box ay sumasaklaw sa magkaibang qubit, na nagbibigay-daan sa samplex optimizer na pagsamahin ang kanilang mga propagation node sa mga shared node. Ipinapakita ito sa seksyon ng trace information.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![../\\_images/f6b6fe7b60a39ba897814008443fa79b66213005462ab09f49ffc89aab1f3668.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/f6b6fe7b60a39ba897814008443fa79b66213005462ab09f49ffc89aab1f3668.avif)\n"
msgstr "![../\\_images/f6b6fe7b60a39ba897814008443fa79b66213005462ab09f49ffc89aab1f3668.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/f6b6fe7b60a39ba897814008443fa79b66213005462ab09f49ffc89aab1f3668.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Barrier labels in the template circuit {#barrier-labels-in-the-template-circuit}"
msgstr "Mga barrier label sa template circuit {#barrier-labels-in-the-template-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calling [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") on the circuit above produces a template whose barriers carry identifying labels. Each label has the form `{side}{scope}@{key=value&...}`:\n"
msgstr "Ang pagtawag sa [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") sa circuit sa itaas ay gumagawa ng template na ang mga barrier ay may mga identifying label. Ang bawat label ay may anyong `{side}{scope}@{key=value&...}`:\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Side**: `L` = left-dressing boundary, `M` = inner box content boundary, `R` = right-dressing boundary.\n"
msgstr "**Panig**: `L` = hangganan ng kaliwang dressing, `M` = hangganan ng nilalaman ng panloob na box, `R` = hangganan ng kanang dressing.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Scope**: An integer index (or underscore-separated list for nested boxes) that distinguishes multiple boxes at the same nesting level.\n"
msgstr "**Scope**: Isang integer index (o listahang pinaghihiwalay ng underscore para sa mga nested na box) na nagpapakilala sa pagitan ng maraming box sa parehong antas ng nesting.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Annotations**: An `@`-prefixed, `&`-separated list of `key=value` pairs derived from the box’s annotations. The `tag` key comes from a [`Tag`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tag#samplomatic.Tag \"samplomatic.Tag\") annotation and `inject_noise` comes from an [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") annotation.\n"
msgstr "**Mga annotation**: Isang listahang nagsisimula sa `@` at pinaghihiwalay ng `&` ng mga pares na `key=value` na hinango mula sa mga annotation ng box. Ang `tag` key ay galing sa isang [`Tag`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tag#samplomatic.Tag \"samplomatic.Tag\") annotation at ang `inject_noise` ay galing sa isang [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") annotation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Barriers from untagged boxes carry only the side and scope (for example, `L2`), with no `@` suffix.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga barrier mula sa mga walang tag na box ay may side at scope lamang (halimbawa, `L2`), na walang `@` suffix.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![../\\_images/e533d70a29504005a636aa27306d3ce3b1d2488358ac6a53f0674f2934698ab8.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/e533d70a29504005a636aa27306d3ce3b1d2488358ac6a53f0674f2934698ab8.avif)\n"
msgstr "![../\\_images/e533d70a29504005a636aa27306d3ce3b1d2488358ac6a53f0674f2934698ab8.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/e533d70a29504005a636aa27306d3ce3b1d2488358ac6a53f0674f2934698ab8.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The barrier labels can also be extracted programmatically:\n"
msgstr "Maaari ring i-extract ang mga barrier label sa programmatic na paraan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trace information on samplex nodes {#trace-information-on-samplex-nodes}"
msgstr "Trace information sa mga samplex node {#trace-information-on-samplex-nodes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Passing `debug=True` to [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") attaches trace information to every samplex node. Each node’s [`trace_info`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-nodes-node#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.Node.trace_info \"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.Node.trace_info\") attribute is a `TraceInfo` object whose `trace_refs` dictionary maps annotation keys (for example, `\"tag\"` and `\"inject_noise\"`) to sets of ref strings. Nodes without a corresponding box annotation have `trace_info=None`.\n"
msgstr "Ang pagpasa ng `debug=True` sa [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") ay nag-aattach ng trace information sa bawat samplex node. Ang attribute na [`trace_info`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-nodes-node#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.Node.trace_info \"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.Node.trace_info\") ng bawat node ay isang `TraceInfo` object na ang `trace_refs` dictionary ay nagmamapa ng mga annotation key (halimbawa, `\"tag\"` at `\"inject_noise\"`) sa mga set ng ref string. Ang mga node na walang katumbas na box annotation ay may `trace_info=None`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When [`draw()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.draw \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.draw\") is called on a debug-built samplex, hovering over any node in the interactive graph reveals its `trace_refs` inside the hover tooltip.\n"
msgstr "Kapag tinawag ang [`draw()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.draw \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.draw\") sa isang samplex na binuo sa debug mode, ang pag-hover sa anumang node sa interactive graph ay naglalantad ng `trace_refs` nito sa loob ng hover tooltip.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trace information can also be inspected programmatically. Notice that some nodes carry references from both `'cx_ab'` and `'cx_cd'`. The samplex optimizer merged their parallel propagation nodes because the two boxes cover disjoint qubits and share a common predecessor from the right-dressed measurement box’s emission.\n"
msgstr "Maaari ring siyasatin ang trace information sa programmatic na paraan. Pansinin na may ilang node na may dalang mga reference mula sa parehong `'cx_ab'` at `'cx_cd'`. Pinagsama ng samplex optimizer ang kanilang mga parallel propagation node dahil ang dalawang box ay sumasaklaw sa magkahiwalay na qubit at may common predecessor mula sa emission ng right-dressed na measurement box.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To find all nodes that originate from a specific box, filter by the `\"tag\"` key:\n"
msgstr "Para hanapin ang lahat ng node na nagmula sa isang partikular na box, mag-filter ayon sa `\"tag\"` key:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The samplex DAG {#the-samplex-dag}"
msgstr "Ang samplex DAG {#the-samplex-dag}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The samplex returned by [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") is a directed acyclic graph (DAG) where **edges denote register dependency**. That is, an edge from node A to node B means B must wait for A to have acted on the shared virtual registers before B is allowed to act. This is not a temporal ordering like the DAG of a quantum circuit. Instead, the graph flows from nodes responsible for generating randomizations to nodes responsible for synthesizing them as outputs.\n"
msgstr "Ang samplex na ibinabalik ng [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") ay isang directed acyclic graph (DAG) kung saan ang **mga edge ay nagsasaad ng register dependency**. Ibig sabihin, ang edge mula node A papuntang node B ay nangangahulugang kailangang maghintay ang B hanggang makapag-act ang A sa mga shared virtual register bago payagang mag-act ang B. Hindi ito temporal na pagkakasunod-sunod tulad ng DAG ng isang quantum circuit. Sa halip, ang graph ay dumadaloy mula sa mga node na responsable sa pagbuo ng mga randomization patungo sa mga node na responsable sa pag-synthesize ng mga ito bilang mga output.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There are three node types, each with a distinct visual style in the interactive plot:\n"
msgstr "May tatlong uri ng node, bawat isa ay may natatanging visual style sa interactive plot:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Shape  | Color         | Type                                                                                                                                                             | Role                                                            |\n"
"| ------ | ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Star   | Red           | [`SamplingNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-nodes-sampling-node#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.SamplingNode \"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.SamplingNode\")         | Instantiates new virtual registers from a distribution or input |\n"
"| Circle | Green         | [`EvaluationNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-nodes-evaluation-node#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.EvaluationNode \"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.EvaluationNode\") | Transforms, combines, or propagates virtual registers           |\n"
"| Bowtie | Blue / Purple | [`CollectionNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-nodes-collection-node#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.CollectionNode \"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.CollectionNode\") | Reads registers and writes to `sample()` outputs                |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Hugis  | Kulay         | Uri                                                                                                                                                              | Papel                                                           |\n"
"| ------ | ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Star   | Red           | [`SamplingNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-nodes-sampling-node#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.SamplingNode \"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.SamplingNode\")         | Gumagawa ng bagong virtual register mula sa distribution o input |\n"
"| Circle | Green         | [`EvaluationNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-nodes-evaluation-node#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.EvaluationNode \"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.EvaluationNode\") | Nagta-transform, nagsasama, o nagpapalaganap ng mga virtual register |\n"
"| Bowtie | Blue / Purple | [`CollectionNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-nodes-collection-node#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.CollectionNode \"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.CollectionNode\") | Nagbabasa ng mga register at nagsusulat sa mga output ng `sample()` |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execution proceeds in three phases:\n"
msgstr "Ang execution ay nagpapatuloy sa tatlong yugto:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "All sampling nodes run first (in parallel).\n"
msgstr "Una munang tumatakbo ang lahat ng sampling node (nang magkakasabay).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Evaluation nodes run next, in topological order (parallel within each generation).\n"
msgstr "Susunod na tumatakbo ang mga evaluation node, sa topological order (magkakasabay sa loob ng bawat henerasyon).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Collection nodes run last (in parallel).\n"
msgstr "Huling tumatakbo ang mga collection node (nang magkakasabay).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The graphviz layout reflects this. Sampling nodes appear at the top, collection nodes at the bottom.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ito ng graphviz layout. Ang mga sampling node ay nasa itaas, ang mga collection node ay nasa ibaba.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hover tooltips {#hover-tooltips}"
msgstr "Mga hover tooltip {#hover-tooltips}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every node in the interactive visualization shows a tooltip when you hover over it. The tooltip contains the following information:\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat node sa interactive visualization ay nagpapakita ng tooltip kapag nag-hover ka rito. Ang tooltip ay naglalaman ng sumusunod na impormasyon:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Node class name** and its integer graph index.\n"
msgstr "**Pangalan ng class ng node** at ang integer graph index nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Register manifests**, which registers the node instantiates, reads from, writes to, and removes. These tell you how data flows between nodes.\n"
msgstr "**Mga register manifest**, kung aling mga register ang ginagawa, binabasa, sinusulatan, at inaalis ng node. Sinasabi nito sa iyo kung paano dumadaloy ang data sa pagitan ng mga node.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Node-specific details**, including the distribution type for sampling nodes, the operand for multiplication nodes, the template parameter indices for collection nodes, and so on.\n"
msgstr "**Mga detalyeng partikular sa node**, kabilang ang uri ng distribution para sa mga sampling node, ang operand para sa mga multiplication node, ang mga template parameter index para sa mga collection node, at iba pa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Trace refs** (only when `debug=True`), which are the annotation keys and ref strings that link the node back to its originating boxes.\n"
msgstr "**Trace refs** (kapag `debug=True` lamang), na mga annotation key at ref string na nag-uugnay sa node pabalik sa mga pinagmulan nitong box.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clicking the plot and then hovering over individual nodes is the fastest way to understand what a given node does without reading source code.\n"
msgstr "Ang pag-click sa plot at pagkatapos ay pag-hover sa mga indibidwal na node ang pinakamabilis na paraan para maunawaan kung ano ang ginagawa ng isang node nang hindi nagbabasa ng source code.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplex summary {#samplex-summary}"
msgstr "Buod ng samplex {#samplex-summary}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before examining the visualization, `print(samplex)` gives a quick text summary of the node count, required inputs, and promised outputs.\n"
msgstr "Bago suriin ang visualization, ang `print(samplex)` ay nagbibigay ng mabilis na text summary ng bilang ng node, mga kinakailangang input, at mga ipinangakong output.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inspect registers {#inspect-registers}"
msgstr "Siyasatin ang mga register {#inspect-registers}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Passing `keep_registers=True` to [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\") retains the intermediate [`VirtualRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/virtual-registers-virtual-register#samplomatic.virtual_registers.VirtualRegister \"samplomatic.virtual_registers.VirtualRegister\") objects that are live at the end of sampling, and stores them in `outputs.metadata[\"registers\"]`. Each register is a 2D array (shape `(num_subsystems, num_randomizations)`, with possible trailing gate-shape dimensions) of virtual group elements.\n"
msgstr "Ang pagpasa ng `keep_registers=True` sa [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\") ay nagpapanatili sa mga intermediate na [`VirtualRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/virtual-registers-virtual-register#samplomatic.virtual_registers.VirtualRegister \"samplomatic.virtual_registers.VirtualRegister\") object na buhay pa sa pagtatapos ng sampling, at iniimbak ang mga ito sa `outputs.metadata[\"registers\"]`. Ang bawat register ay isang 2D array (hugis `(num_subsystems, num_randomizations)`, na may posibleng trailing na gate-shape dimension) ng mga virtual group element.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is useful for verifying that virtual gates were combined correctly, or for inspecting the raw Pauli or unitary samples before they are synthesized into rotation angles.\n"
msgstr "Kapaki-pakinabang ito para i-verify na tama ang pagkakasama-sama ng mga virtual gate, o para siyasatin ang raw na Pauli o unitary sample bago i-synthesize ang mga ito bilang mga rotation angle.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can view the contents of the end-state of a particular register. In the following example, the register has type [`PauliRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/virtual-registers-pauli-register#samplomatic.virtual_registers.PauliRegister \"samplomatic.virtual_registers.PauliRegister\"). See the `API documentation(/apidocs/index)`\\_\\_ for details about the storage format.\n"
msgstr "Maaari mong tingnan ang nilalaman ng end-state ng isang partikular na register. Sa sumusunod na halimbawa, ang register ay may uri na [`PauliRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/virtual-registers-pauli-register#samplomatic.virtual_registers.PauliRegister \"samplomatic.virtual_registers.PauliRegister\"). Tingnan ang `API documentation(/apidocs/index)`\\_\\_ para sa mga detalye tungkol sa storage format.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "How samplex nodes map to template parameters {#how-samplex-nodes-map-to-template-parameters}"
msgstr "Kung paano nagmamapa ang mga samplex node sa mga template parameter {#how-samplex-nodes-map-to-template-parameters}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `outputs[\"parameter_values\"]` array returned by [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\") has shape `(num_randomizations, N)`, where `N` matches `len(template.parameters)`. Each column corresponds to one parameter in the template circuit — the i-th column fills in `template.parameters[i]`.\n"
msgstr "Ang array na `outputs[\"parameter_values\"]` na ibinabalik ng [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\") ay may hugis na `(num_randomizations, N)`, kung saan ang `N` ay tumutugma sa `len(template.parameters)`. Ang bawat column ay tumutugma sa isang parameter sa template circuit — pinupunan ng i-th na column ang `template.parameters[i]`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`CollectTemplateValues`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-nodes-collect-template-values#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.CollectTemplateValues \"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.CollectTemplateValues\") collection nodes are the link between virtual registers and template parameters. Each such node holds index information that records which columns of the output array it writes to. This makes it possible to trace which virtual gate subsystems drive which template parameters.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga collection node na [`CollectTemplateValues`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-nodes-collect-template-values#samplomatic.samplex.nodes.CollectTemplateValues \"samplomatic.samplex.nodes.CollectTemplateValues\") ang ugnayan sa pagitan ng mga virtual register at mga template parameter. Ang bawat ganoong node ay may hawak na index information na nagtatala kung aling mga column ng output array ang sinusulatan nito. Dahil dito, posibleng matunton kung aling mga virtual gate subsystem ang nagpapatakbo sa aling mga template parameter.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "See the \\{Samplex inputs and outputs}`samplex-io` guide to learn how to bind the sampled parameter values to the template circuit and run experiments.\n"
msgstr "Tingnan ang guide na \\{Samplex inputs and outputs}`samplex-io` para malaman kung paano i-bind ang mga sampled na parameter value sa template circuit at magpatakbo ng mga experiment.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Automatic tagging {#automatic-tagging}"
msgstr "Awtomatikong pag-tag {#automatic-tagging}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When using [`generate_boxing_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/transpiler-generate-boxing-pass-manager#samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager \"samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager\"), the `add_tags` parameter automatically adds [`Tag`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tag#samplomatic.Tag \"samplomatic.Tag\") annotations to all boxes. Three modes are available:\n"
msgstr "Kapag gumagamit ng [`generate_boxing_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/transpiler-generate-boxing-pass-manager#samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager \"samplomatic.transpiler.generate_boxing_pass_manager\"), ang parameter na `add_tags` ay awtomatikong nagdaragdag ng mga [`Tag`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tag#samplomatic.Tag \"samplomatic.Tag\") annotation sa lahat ng box. May tatlong mode na available:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`\"unique_instance\"`**: Assigns sequential `ref` (`t0`, `t1`, and so on) to boxes in circuit order. Every box gets a distinct `ref` regardless of its structure.\n"
msgstr "**`\"unique_instance\"`**: Nagtatalaga ng sunud-sunod na `ref` (`t0`, `t1`, at iba pa) sa mga box ayon sa pagkakasunod sa circuit. Bawat box ay may natatanging `ref` anuman ang istruktura nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`\"unique_box\"`**: Computes a structural hash of each box’s content and assigns the same `ref` to all structurally equivalent boxes. This is useful for grouping boxes by type rather than position.\n"
msgstr "**`\"unique_box\"`**: Kinakalkula ang structural hash ng nilalaman ng bawat box at nagtatalaga ng parehong `ref` sa lahat ng box na magkapareho ang istruktura. Kapaki-pakinabang ito sa pag-group ng mga box ayon sa uri sa halip na ayon sa posisyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`\"noise_ref\"`**: Copies the `ref` from each box’s [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") annotation and only tags boxes that have one. This is useful when meaningful noise refs already exist.\n"
msgstr "**`\"noise_ref\"`**: Kinokopya ang `ref` mula sa [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") annotation ng bawat box at tina-tag lang ang mga box na mayroon nito. Kapaki-pakinabang ito kapag may mga makabuluhang noise ref na.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following example applies `\"unique_instance\"` and `\"unique_box\"` to a circuit whose two CX boxes are structurally equivalent. With `\"unique_instance\"`, each gets a distinct `ref`, while with `\"unique_box\"`, they share one.\n"
msgstr "Ang sumusunod na halimbawa ay nag-a-apply ng `\"unique_instance\"` at `\"unique_box\"` sa isang circuit na ang dalawang CX box ay magkapareho ang istruktura. Sa `\"unique_instance\"`, bawat isa ay may natatanging `ref`, samantalang sa `\"unique_box\"`, iisa ang ibinabahagi nila.\n"
